~ start
Premier Bagnasco: You are only the second French president to dine at the Quirinal in a decade. The first was remembered mainly for the wine.
- Ask for their support in the council [#id:council_support] => council_support
- Speak only of culture [#id:culture_only] => culture_only
~ council_support
Premier Bagnasco: Rome's vote is old, patient, and rarely free. Name the file, and name what France can do for the Mezzogiorno.
- Promise the infrastructure package [#id:promise_package] => promise_package
- Offer only goodwill [#id:goodwill] => goodwill
~ promise_package
Premier Bagnasco: Then Italy will look kindly on your file, and the south will have its railway, or the renderings of one.
=> END
~ goodwill
Premier Bagnasco: Goodwill is welcome at this table, but it does not move votes. We will drink to it anyway.
=> END
~ culture_only
Premier Bagnasco: A wise choice. The treaties that last are the ones nobody had to vote on.
- Propose a restorations fund [#id:restorations] => restorations
- Let the evening end [#id:evening_ends] => evening_ends
~ restorations
Premier Bagnasco: For the abbeys and the aqueducts both. Europe began as a culture and only later learned to file paperwork.
=> END
~ evening_ends
Premier Bagnasco: In that case: to the friendship, and to the wine, which tonight at least is entirely Italian.
=> END
